      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In continuation of investigations on primary hyperlipidaemias, we determined serum thromboxane (TX) B2 and prostaglandin (PG) F2 alpha after standardized blood clotting in patients without hyperlipidaemia and without (group 1, n = 11) or with coronary heart disease (CHD; group 2, n = 5), in patients with familial combined hyperlipoproteinaemia and without (group 3, n = 4) or with CHD (group 4, n = 5), as well as in patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia and CHD (group 5, n = 5). TXB2 was detected by gas chromatography and PGF2 alpha by means of radioimmunoassay. The TXB2 level did not differ significantly between the groups, but there was a tendency to higher values in hyperlipidaemia, while in group 5 the level tended to decrease with rising serum LDL-cholesterol and in group 3 it tended to increase with rising serum apolipoprotein B. The PGF2 alpha level was significantly lower in group 4 than in groups 1 and 3. It showed in group 5 a negative correlation with serum LDL-cholesterol and in group 3 a positive correlation with serum triglycerides."},
